Release Debian 2.0.1 Alpha1

Fix a bug where code_dark_configurator restarts (attempts) cdpw, not
orthanc. Hangover from when we had our own orthanc paackage.

Release Debian 2.0 Alpha1

No cdpw changes as such. Debian now changes to just using the latest
official kernel as the default. This allows us Z2 (Intel Graphics) and
Nvidia and Barco 6700 cards.  Other Barco cards won't work, but we can
avoid having to disable secure mode.  We still will keep the modified
kernel as an alternate boot.

Release Debian 2.0 Dev1

Move cdpw-ohif into a separate repository - build it separate.
It is an important but not *dependent* package for us. This
means we can flatten the build here to just the scriptage
and dependency graphs.

Release Debian 2.0 Dev0

Debian 13, one piece of media approach. No waiting for CODE_DARK
to be mounted.

No internal changes to Orthanc any more so we only actually need
to build cdpw-ohif.

